prompt:
Use show_view with view "ui", spec {root,elements} and named sources. root is a string key. elements MUST be an OBJECT keyed by element IDs, never an array or nested tree. Example: {"root":"chart","elements":{"chart":{"type":"Line","props":{"title":"Trend","summary":"Trend","data":{"$state":"/sources/sales/rows"},"x":"date","y":"amount"},"children":[]}}}. Each element has type, props and children. Use an empty children array for leaves. All elements must form one tree.
Never provide initial state, actions, repeats, conditions, sample data or literal numeric values. Data props must be {$state:"/sources/name/path"}. The server resolves these paths. The model writes words and arranges components.
Stack: Groups its children. Title digits must match resolved data or applied parameters. Props: { title?: string }
Grid: Groups its children. Title digits must match resolved data or applied parameters. Props: { title?: string, columns?: "one" | "two" | "three" }
Card: Groups its children. Title digits must match resolved data or applied parameters. Props: { title?: string }
Section: Groups its children. Title digits must match resolved data or applied parameters. Props: { title?: string }
Tabs: Groups its children. Title digits must match resolved data or applied parameters. Props: { title?: string }
Accordion: Groups its children. Title digits must match resolved data or applied parameters. Props: { title?: string }
Divider: Separates sections Props: {  }
Heading: Model prose. Number words are allowed; digit quantities must match resolved data or applied parameters. Alphanumeric identifiers such as Q3 are allowed. Props: { text: string, tone?: "info" | "warning" | "success" }
